1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:06,900
Remember that scientist you met?
From a conversation to a team pack, with fictional (Demo) researchers.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:20,900
Seven steps, one real workflow.
Your notes stay in this browser by default. Download a backup file before you rely on them.

3
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:36,900
Save scientific contacts.
Paste ORCID iDs and name the meeting. Each public record is read once, on your request, and tagged.

4
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:54,900
Or save one person at a time.
Save as contact asks first, reads the public record once, and does not follow or notify the person.

5
00:00:55,400 --> 00:01:09,900
Remember the conversation.
Your notes stay in this browser by default. They are not part of anyone's public record.

6
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:25,900
Keep your promises.
A follow-up with a due date, listed with everything you owe people. No invitation or notification sent.

7
00:01:26,400 --> 00:01:41,900
Turn contacts into working groups.
A group you curate in this browser. Curated membership/project attribution is not independently verified.

8
00:01:42,400 --> 00:01:55,900
Choose what belongs to the project.
Selecting an output records your decision. It does not change ORCID or confirm authorship.

9
00:01:56,400 --> 00:02:09,900
Organize the science.
Roster, bibliography and member biosketches in one file. Contact tags, notes and follow-ups are not included.

10
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:20,900
Every step completed in the app.
The team pack is a file on this device. You decide whether to share it.

11
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:29,900
Try Science Record Player.
